 "description": "Own Bitcoin server, settings and fetch rules (Android AddressServerRules.kt, iOS AddressServerRules.swift). «clamp»: too long input (e.g. pasted) is cut to AddressServer.MAX_LENGTH + 1 (201) instead of being dropped, so the check still sees that it was too long; «problem» = AddressServer.check(output).problem (null = valid or empty): 201/250 otherwise valid characters → INVALID, exactly 200 → valid (same on both platforms) — inputs are ASCII; leading whitespace (space, tab, newline) is dropped first (the check trims it, otherwise « » + 201 would pass as 200). «hostKey»: entry → key for pauses/blocks. «own»: Bitcoin entries are the own server (https:// base) → never blocked 6 h after 403/451 (only the short ExchangeBackoff pause). «testShown»: test result (with its tested url) is shown only for the current checked input url. «confirmPublic»: switching from an own server to public nodes (next = null) asks first when Bitcoin addresses or xpub are watched (btcCount, or «chains» → btcCount(chains); chains null = list not readable → ask). «btcCount»: watched Bitcoin entries by chain list; chains null = list not readable → 1 (ask rather than switch silently).",
